---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { buildToolAlternates } from '../lib/i18n';

const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "WebPage",
  "url": "https://onlineaudiotest.com/privacy/",
  "name": "Privacy Policy — OnlineAudioTest.com",
  "description": "Privacy policy for OnlineAudioTest.com, including browser audio processing, analytics, cookies, and contact form data.",
  "inLanguage": "en-US",
  "dateModified": "2026-10-11",
  "isPartOf": { "@type": "WebSite", "url": "https://onlineaudiotest.com/", "name": "OnlineAudioTest.com" },
  "publisher": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "OnlineAudioTest.com", "url": "https://onlineaudiotest.com/", "logo": "https://onlineaudiotest.com/icon.png" }
};
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy — OnlineAudioTest.com"
  description="Privacy policy for OnlineAudioTest.com, including browser audio processing, analytics, cookies, and contact form data."
  canonical="https://onlineaudiotest.com/privacy/"
  alternates={buildToolAlternates('/privacy/', '/pt-br/privacidade/')}
  schema={schema}
>

  <div class="policy-page container">
    <div class="policy-inner">

      <header class="policy-header">
        <span class="eyebrow">Legal</span>
        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="policy-meta">Last updated: <time datetime="2026-10-11">October 11, 2026</time></p>
      </header>

      <div class="policy-body">

        <section>
          <h2>Overview</h2>
          <p>OnlineAudioTest.com ("we", "our", or "the site") is a free, browser-based suite of audio diagnostic tools. We are committed to protecting your privacy. This policy explains what data we collect (if any), how we use it, and what rights you have.</p>
          <p>The audio tools process microphone input and generated sounds in your browser. The tool code does not upload audio or test result values. The site does load third-party analytics scripts, which can receive page usage and technical information as described below.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Information We Collect</h2>
          <h3>Audio Data</h3>
          <p>The audio tool code processes microphone input and generated sounds in your browser and does not upload audio or test result values. Microphone access is controlled by your browser. Separate from the tools, third-party analytics scripts load on the site and may collect information about page visits and the browser or device.</p>

          <h3>Usage Data (Analytics)</h3>
          <p>The site currently loads Google Analytics and Ahrefs Web Analytics. Google Analytics may process page URLs, usage events, referral information, and technical details such as browser or device information; Google documents that Analytics can use cookies and that browsers may send the page URL and IP address to Google. Ahrefs says its Web Analytics product uses no cookies or persistent identifiers by default and reports aggregated traffic trends. See <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites?hl=en-in" rel="noopener noreferrer">how Google uses information from sites that use its services</a>, <a href="https://support.google.com/analytics/answer/12159447?hl=en" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Analytics data collection</a>, and <a href="https://help.ahrefs.com/en/articles/10247870-about-ahrefs-web-analytics" rel="noopener noreferrer">Ahrefs Web Analytics data collection</a>.</p>

          <h3>Cookies</h3>
          <p>Google Analytics may use cookies or similar technologies depending on browser and configuration. Ahrefs Web Analytics says it does not use cookies or persistent identifiers by default. Third-party services may process information through their own technologies.</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Analytics:</strong> To understand page visits and site usage.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>You can manage cookies through your browser settings. Blocking third-party scripts or cookies may affect analytics and may affect other embedded or site features, but the core audio tools are designed to run in the browser.</p>

          <h3>Contact Forms</h3>
          <p>If you contact us via the contact form, we receive the information you submit, such as your name, email address, and message. The form is handled through the site hosting/form infrastructure. We use submissions to respond and operate support; provider processing and retention may also apply.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>How We Use Your Information</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>To operate and improve the audio testing tools</li>
            <li>To respond to support requests and inquiries</li>
            <li>To measure site performance and diagnose technical issues</li>
          </ul>
          <p>We do not sell personal information. Analytics providers process information under their own terms and privacy policies. We do not currently describe advertising services here because advertising code was not found in the site layout reviewed for this policy.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Third-Party Services</h2>
          <p>The site currently loads these third-party analytics services, which have their own terms and privacy policies:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Google Analytics</strong> — site usage measurement</li>
            <li><strong>Ahrefs Web Analytics</strong> — aggregated site usage measurement</li>
          </ul>
          <p>We encourage you to review the privacy policies of these third parties.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Data Retention</h2>
          <p>Audio and test result values are not uploaded by the audio tool code. Analytics providers and the hosting/form provider may retain information according to their own policies and configuration. Contact us through the <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a> with a data request.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
          <p>OnlineAudioTest.com is not directed at children under the age of 13. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children. If you believe a child has provided personal information through our site, please contact us so we can delete it.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Your Rights</h2>
          <p>Depending on your location, you may have the right to:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Access the personal data we hold about you</li>
            <li>Request correction or deletion of your data</li>
            <li>Object to or restrict certain processing of your data</li>
            <li>Lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority (for EEA residents)</li>
          </ul>
          <p>To exercise any of these rights, contact us at the address below.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
          <p>We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. When we do, we will revise the "Last updated" date at the top. We encourage you to review this page periodically.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Contact</h2>
          <p>If you have questions or concerns about this Privacy Policy, please contact us via the <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a>.</p>
        </section>

      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

</Layout>

<style>
  .policy-page {
    padding-top: var(--s-4xl);
    padding-bottom: var(--s-5xl);
  }
  .policy-inner {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }
  .policy-header {
    margin-bottom: var(--s-2xl);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--s-sm);
  }
  .policy-header h1 {
    font-size: 36px;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -1.5px;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .policy-meta {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--mute);
  }
  .policy-body {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--s-2xl);
  }
  .policy-body section {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--s-md);
    padding-bottom: var(--s-2xl);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);
  }
  .policy-body section:last-child {
    border-bottom: none;
  }
  .policy-body h2 {
    font-size: 20px;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.5px;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .policy-body h3 {
    font-size: 15px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--ink);
    margin-top: var(--s-xs);
  }
  .policy-body p {
    font-size: 15px;
    color: var(--body-text);
    line-height: 1.75;
  }
  .policy-body ul {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--s-xs);
    padding-left: var(--s-lg);
    list-style: disc;
  }
  .policy-body li {
    font-size: 15px;
    color: var(--body-text);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .policy-body a {
    color: var(--link);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }
  strong { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 500; }
</style>
